---
description: TidyMac Windows product, platform-safety, MCP and documentation rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow the root `AGENTS.md`; it is the single source of truth. Before changing Windows behavior, read the relevant contract under `../tidymac-docs/features/` and the implementation companion under `docs/windows/`.

- Keep proposals distinct from code and test evidence. Never claim an MCP call or test passed unless you observed its result.
- Use synthetic fixture trees for mutation tests; never clean a real user profile.
- Preserve explicit review, scan-bound identities, Recycle Bin recovery and no arbitrary shell/PowerShell rules.
- Do not silently block websites/ads, inspect browser profiles, move system/app/profile data, install drivers, capture screens, or change activation/licensing.
- Use official Windows/browser handoffs and plain-language uncertainty. Broad permissions or old files/drivers are not proof of harm.
- Include privacy, failure, cancellation, recovery, performance and measurable acceptance criteria in new feature specs.
